{"name":"Mount Olympus","hex":"#d4ffff","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mount","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hill or mountain.","Any of seven fleshy prominences in the palm of the hand, taken to represent the influences of various heavenly bodies."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An animal, usually a horse, used to ride on.","A car, bicycle, or motorcycle used for racing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mount"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mount Olympus","blocks":[{"text":"Mount Olympus is an extensive massif near the Thermaic Gulf of the Aegean Sea, in Greece, located on the border between Thessaly and Macedonia, between the regional units of Larissa and Pieria, about 80 km (50 mi) southwest from Thessaloniki. Mount Olympus has 52 peaks and deep gorges.\nThe highest peak, Mytikas, meaning \"nose\", rises to 2,917.727 metres (9,572.60 ft) and is the highest peak in Greece, and one of the highest peaks in Europe in terms of topographic prominence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Olympus_National_Park_30.jpg/330px-Olympus_National_Park_30.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Olympus","wikidata":"Q80344"},{"title":"Mount Olympus (Washington)","blocks":[{"text":"Mount Olympus, at 7,980 feet (2,430 m), is the tallest and most prominent mountain in the Olympic Mountains of the U.S. state of Washington. Located on the Olympic Peninsula, it is also a central feature of Olympic National Park. Mount Olympus is the highest summit of the Olympic Mountains; however, peaks such as Mount Constance and The Brothers, on the eastern margin of the range, are better known, being visible from the Seattle metropolitan area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Mt_Olympus.jpg/330px-Mt_Olympus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Olympus_(Washington)","wikidata":"Q522586"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Mytikas_peak_02.jpg/500px-Mytikas_peak_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Mytikas_peak_02.jpg/1280px-Mytikas_peak_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Mytikas_peak_02.jpg/500px-Mytikas_peak_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mytikas: the highest peak","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMytikas_peak_02.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Olympus_Mountain.jpg/500px-Olympus_Mountain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Olympus_Mountain.jpg/1280px-Olympus_Mountain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Olympus_Mountain.jpg/500px-Olympus_Mountain.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stratospheric view of Mount Olympus","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOlympus_Mountain.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Refuge_Giosos_Apostolidis_Olympus_National_Park_Greece.jpg/500px-Refuge_Giosos_Apostolidis_Olympus_National_Park_Greece.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Refuge_Giosos_Apostolidis_Olympus_National_Park_Greece.jpg/1280px-Refuge_Giosos_Apostolidis_Olympus_National_Park_Greece.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Refuge_Giosos_Apostolidis_O